id to be quested when their sides have been crushed by each other, or so joined to them as thence to be less baked. North."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"(2) To give tongue as hounds do on trail. \" To bay or quest as a dog,\" Florio, p. 1. Still in use. See Forby, ii. 268.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":234.572487931958,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":25.438439999999996,"r":178.35594512,"t":257.93356539999996},"charspan":[0,118],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/22","text":"(2) To give tongue as hounds do on trail. \" To bay or quest as a dog,\" Florio, p. 1. Still in use. See Forby, ii. 268."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Kenettes questade to quelle, Al so breme so any belle. The deer daunteden in the dclle,","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":214.2529048379472,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":53.751279999999994,"r":144.14943536000004,"t":232.9693841536},"charspan":[0,87],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/23","text":"Kenettes questade to quelle, Al so breme so any belle. The deer daunteden in the dclle,"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"That al the downe deuede.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":207.44385771192367,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":54.6136,"r":130.21060744000005,"t":212.41833533839997},"charspan":[0,25],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/24","text":"That al the downe deuede."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Reliq. Antiq. il. 7. (Z) An inquest. Var. dial Both words are used by Hall, Henry VIU. ff. 50, 53.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":184.2712695813965,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":26.875639999999997,"r":179.21970231999995,"t":206.20924616879995},"charspan":[0,98],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/25","text":"Reliq. Antiq. il. 7. (Z) An inquest. Var. dial Both words are used by Hall, Henry VIU. ff. 50, 53."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig"